Drop the Ripgrep WORKSPACE stanzas the public mirror cannot satisfy

WORKSPACE.linux loads //Vendors/Ripgrep:repositories.bzl, but Vendors/Ripgrep is
absent from SYNCLIST, so the public mirror never receives the directory. A
WORKSPACE load() is eager, so every commit from 3dc01fe5 onward fails at load
phase for anyone building the community repo. Nothing outside the two WORKSPACE
files names ripgrep, so removing the load, the ripgrep_repositories() call and
the @ripgrep_crates load costs the Linux build nothing.
